# KNOWN GAP `todo/t1309` — a nested `Box[Box[R]]` LEAKS ITS INNER BOX AT SCOPE
# EXIT. Blocked on `todo/t0096`.
#
# ⚠ CONSTRUCTION ONLY, DELIBERATELY: the box is built and NEVER READ. That is
# what makes this a repro for the LEAK rather than for `todo/t1077`'s read
# defect — `t1077` is fixed and every nested-`Box` READ is correct now, but the
# drop chain still never reaches the inner box.
#
# ⚠ THE PAYLOAD IS HEAP-FORCED (`mk(a, b)`, and the halves are long enough to
# defeat any small-buffer optimization). A `.rodata` literal payload is an
# immortal view and leaks nothing, so a fixture written with `"hi"` would be
# ASan-clean and pin NOTHING.
#
# ⛔ MECHANISM: UNDETERMINED. The obvious candidate was measured and REJECTED —
# `todo/t1077`'s fix changes `deref_type` from `T` to `Box__T`, and
# `deref_type` gates the deep-clone branch, so a plausible story was that it
# now selects a clone that leaks. It does not:
#   * `--clones=sites`: 1 implicit clone (`String`, CoW materialization) before
#     the fix and the identical 1 after — same count, same type;
#   * emitted C: no `Box__GorgetString__clone` in either state; both carry one
#     `gorget_string_clone_to_owned` and the two construction `box_alloc`s;
#   * ASan: this construction-only program reports the SAME records and the
#     SAME byte count before and after the fix;
#   * and structurally it cannot fire — `is_resource_type` matches
#     `GirType::Named(name)` with `is_resource_name(name)`, which does not
#     admit `Box__GorgetString`
#     (`grep -n 'pub fn is_resource_type' -A 4 src/ir/types.rs`).
# The leak is PRE-EXISTING and independent of the read fix. What IS known is
# where the drop is declined: `grep -n 'DS::Trivial(_) => None' src/lir/lower/drops.rs`
# — routing the outer box's drop through the inner `Box__R__drop` wrapper is
# the natural fix and trips `todo/t0096`'s `Box__R__drop` redefinition.
#
# EXPECTED: prints `built`, exits 0, AND IS LEAK-CLEAN under
# `gg build --sanitize`. It is the last clause that fails today.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    Box[Box[String]] w = Box[Box[String]](Box[String](mk("aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa", "bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb")))
    print("built")
